  "label": "Mapping of 'blacks are musical' to the Black man in the struggle",
  "description": "The top text 'blacks are musical' is mapped onto the visual entity 'man_on_left' (the Black man in the suit). The meme uses his physical presence and the context of the struggle to visually represent the stereotype that Black people are 'musical' — a racialized trope that reduces their identity to a simplistic cultural association. The visual of the man being grabbed by the collar is juxtaposed with the text to imply that his 'musicality' is inherently linked to physicality or aggression, aligning with the stereotype 'anti_black_stereotype_aggressive_violent_nature'.",
